      },
      "text": "**Exchange proof sketch**: let O be any optimal solution and g the\nearliest-finishing activity. If O does not contain g, swap O's first activity for g\n— g finishes no later, so it cannot conflict with anything O scheduled after, and\n|O| is unchanged. Repeat. So a greedy solution is as large as any optimal one. ∎"
    },
